===Return to your private bath chamber and discuss the present circumstances with Dan Heng{{subst:void|<!--104020106-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location="Eternal Holy City" Okhema|update|After ensuring Phainon's safety, (Trailblazer) and I retreated to the bath chamber to rest. We also drew our own conclusions about the present situation in the world of Amphoreus}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Unused &mdash; EnterDistrict_G288)
:{{tx}}
::'''Dan Heng:''' An "unspeakable" thing of "unknown origin"... What comes to your mind when we put these keywords together?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} A Stellaron?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' That's right. If you think about the various characteristics of Amphoreus &mdash; an isolated world of eternal night being eroded by an unknown power... we cannot discount this possibility.
:::An Aeon?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' That's right. If you think about the various characteristics of Amphoreus &mdash; an isolated world of eternal night being eroded by an unknown power... we cannot discount this possibility.
:::Uhh... a Leviathan? A cosmic mega octopus?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} An Aeon?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' That's right. If you think about the various characteristics of Amphoreus &mdash; an isolated world of eternal night being eroded by an unknown power... we cannot discount this possibility.
:::Uhh... a Leviathan? A cosmic mega octopus?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Uhh... a Leviathan? A cosmic mega octopus?
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...A hypothesis like that has never occurred to me, I must admit. But considering how the Leviathan hasn't been sighted in the universe for hundreds of Amber Eras, I think the possibility of it being the culprit is minuscule.
::'''Dan Heng:''' Let's think about the various characteristics of Amphoreus instead. An isolated world of eternal night being eroded by an unknown power...
::'''Dan Heng:''' This has been bothering me for a while now. Everything we have seen thus far suggests that Amphoreus wasn't always isolated from the rest of the universe. Be it the birth of the Titans or the encroaching black tide, none of these can be explained as a "natural progression" of a civilization.
::'''Dan Heng:''' There must be other reasons for its current state of isolation. It's just... if the Cancer of All Worlds is truly the culprit, then we should have observed certain phenomena &mdash; explicit or otherwise &mdash; by now, but that isn't the case.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The Voice of the Stellaron?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' That's what I was thinking too. From past experience, the Stellaron within you should be able to resonate with other Stellarons, but we haven't encountered anything like that here.
:::The Antimatter Legion?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' That's what I was thinking too. From past experience, the Destruction has always been involved in some way when it comes to a world corrupted by a Stellaron.
:::The Stellaron Hunters?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The Antimatter Legion?
:::'''Dan Heng:''' That's what I was thinking too. From past experience, the Destruction has always been involved in some way when it comes to a world corrupted by a Stellaron.
:::The Stellaron Hunters?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} The Stellaron Hunters?
::'''Dan Heng:''' That's what I was thinking too. From past experience, Stellaron Hunters are certain to appear on a world with a Stellaron.
::'''Dan Heng:''' There are several other unanswered questions, too. My gut feeling is that things here are not as simple as they seem...
::'''Dan Heng:''' Furthermore, what happened in Penacony also proved that the appearance of a world may not necessarily be due to the influence of just one Path.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No sweat! The Trailblaze can tackle even ten Paths if it must!
:::'''Dan Heng:''' *sigh* It's good to be motivated at least.
:::It could be an all-star cast.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' Heh... In another sense, it's Penacony all over again.
:::Who knows, maybe Akivili's behind it all.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} It could be an all-star cast.
:::'''Dan Heng:''' Heh... In another sense, it's Penacony all over again.
:::Who knows, maybe Akivili's behind it all.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Who knows, maybe Akivili's behind it all.
::'''Dan Heng:''' ...Not even the History Fictionologists would dare to spin a tale like that.
::'''Dan Heng:''' For now, let's just take things as they come. The black tide could be a good starting point. Since {{Rubi|Nikador|Strife Titan}} has fallen, those who were suppressed by them will no doubt begin to counterattack now.
::{{tx}}
:'''Dan Heng:''' The black tide...
